  "summary_md": "The furnishings sector grapples with soft housing-linked demand, yet a theme of margin defense emerges: COOK, HOFT, and FGI improved profits via cost actions and tariff strategies even as sales lag. Balance-sheet repair and shareholder returns—BSET’s dividend hike, FLXS’s debt-free buybacks—underscore a shift to financial resilience. Several narratives break from the pack. AMWD’s merger with MasterBrand closed and the stock will delist, consolidating cabinetry. ATER abandoned legacy e-commerce to pivot into critical-minerals trading and AI exploration in Africa. SNBR narrowly avoided a liquidity crisis, amended covenants, and is exploring capital-structure options, the batch’s most acute stress case. Meanwhile, COOK’s sell-through turned positive and management raised margin guidance, while FLXS extended its industry-beating growth streak. An outlier: NCL reported travel bookings and cruise ship deliveries, a departure from the furnishings peer set.",
  "summary_date": "2026-05-29"
